 36MG    PB(37MG,36MGG)                2014KO14                  ENSDF    202106
 36MG  H TYP=FUL$AUT=BALRAJ SINGH$CIT=ENSDF$CUT=21-MAY-2021$                    
 36MG  H TYP=FUL$AUT=BALRAJ SINGH$CIT=ENSDF$CUT=12-MAR-2019$                    
 36MG c  Includes C({+37}Mg,{+36}Mg|g)                                          
 36MG c  This dataset is adapted from a dataset in the XUNDL database compiled  
 36MG2c  by J.C. Batchelder (ORNL), December 10, 2014                           
 36MG c  Coulomb and nuclear dominated one-neutron removal reaction.            
 36MG c  2014Ko14: {+37}Mg secondary beam was produced in {+9}Be({+48}Ca,X),    
 36MG2c  E=345 MeV/nucleon primary reaction at RIBF-RIKEN facility, using 15 mm 
 36MG3c  thick {+9}Be target. Secondary fragments were selected using           
 36MG4c  B|r-|DE-B|r method through the BigRIPS fragment separator.             
 36MG5c  Beam energies at mid target were 244 MeV/nucleon for the Pb target of  
 36MG6c  3.37 g/cm{+2} thickness, and 240 MeV/nucleon for the C target of       
 36MG7c  2.54 g/cm{+2} thickness. Outgoing {+36}Mg residues were identified     
 36MG8c  using B|r-|DE-tof method with the ZeroDegree spectrometer (ZDS).       
 36MG9c  The |g rays were detected using DALI2 array of 186 NaI(Tl) detectors.  
 36MGAc  Measured E|g, I|g, cross sections, |g rays in coincidence with         
 36MGCc  {+36}Mg outgoing particles, and parallel momentum distributions of     
 36MGDc  {+36}Mg residues. Deduced level and J|p in {+36}Mg.                    
 36MGEc  Comparison with shell-model calculations.                              
 36MG c  Measured total |s=660 mb {I40} for Pb target, and 80 mb {I4} for       
 36MG2c  C target; deduced Coulomb breakup |s=490 mb {I50} for Pb               
 36MG3c  target (2014Ko14)                                                      
